# This machine's checkout has core.autocrlf = true, so git rewrites line endings
# on anything its heuristic calls text. That is fine for prose and source, and it
# is not fine for two things:
#
#   - Fixtures whose whole value is being byte-for-byte what a server sent. A
#     single rewritten byte makes a gzipped page undecompressable. The sibling
#     auction project learned this one the expensive way.
#   - Data files a test pins. Line endings are part of the bytes a checksum or a
#     round-trip test sees, and a rewrite shows up as a failure with no cause in
#     the diff.
#
# Say so explicitly rather than trusting the guess.

*.gz     binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.png    binary

# CSVs are the data spine once entry exists. Pin them to LF so a round-trip
# through a tool, an export or an editor cannot quietly change every line.
*.csv    text eol=lf
